Usage: ./ifm_mpi <options>
GENERAL options:
    -h, --help                    This help.

INPUT options:
    -c, --cellsize=SIZE           DEM cell size, in meters (default: 90)
    -d, --dem=FILE                DEM file
    -l, --landuse=FILE            Landuse file
    -L, --landuse-map=FILE        Landuse file (optional)
    -m, --mask=FILE               Mask file
    -o, --outlet=FILE             Outlet file
    -O, --outdir=DIR              Output directory (default: ./)
    -p, --precipitation=FILE      Precipitation file
    -w, --watch=FILE              Optional list of coordinates to watch
    -H, --soil-hc=FILE            Soil hydraulic conductivity file
    -P, --soil-ph=FILE            Soil pressure head file
    -E, --soil-ep=FILE            Soil effective porosity file

SIMULATION options:
    -b, --tbegin=NUM_SECONDS      Simulation start time (default: 0)
    -f, --tfinal=NUM_SECONDS      Simulation end time (default: 1800)
    -r, --output-rate=NUM_SECONDS How often to output depth files (default: 300)
    -s, --tstep=NUM_SECONDS       Time step in seconds (default: 1)
    -S, --state=FILE              Save/restore simulation state from the given file

ENVIRONMENT options:
    -R, --resourceMap=FILE        Resource map file (default: resources.map)

UNIFORM precipitation file example:
0    100
3599 100
3600 0

NETCDF precipitation file example:
0       wrfout_d04_2010-04-07_00:00:00
600     wrfout_d04_2010-04-07_00:10:00
1200    wrfout_d04_2010-04-07_00:20:00

WATCH file example:
# Lat Lon : Location name
-81.584575 28.413437 : Walt Disney World

